    "title": "Hope On Unshakable Love",
    "summary": "",
    "body": "Today’s meditation invites us to see Hope On Unshakable Love through the gospel. This is not an abstract doctrine, but truth for ordinary fears, relationships, temptations, and decisions.\n\nSin bends our interpretation of life. We defend ourselves, seek visible control, compare ourselves with others, and ask created things to give what only God can give.\n\nChrist meets us with deeper grace. He bears our guilt, becomes our righteousness, brings us near to the Father, and gives the Spirit to form new obedience in us.\n\nSo today, bring your real heart to God. Repent without hiding, receive grace without presumption, and depend on Christ for faithful obedience in the small places of life.\n\nPrayer\n\nFather, praise you for your wise mercy. Forgive my sin and self-trust. Thank you for Christ, my righteousness and hope. Holy Spirit, help me repent, trust, and obey today. In Jesus’ name, amen."
